# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages / Render static sites.
#
# Every real route is prerendered to its own HTML file, so this catch-all is only reached by a
# URL that does not exist. It therefore answers 404 rather than 200: serving the app shell with
# a 200 for an unknown URL is a "soft 404", which Google reports as an error and which lets junk
# URLs get indexed under the home page's title.
#
# Client-side navigation is unaffected, the router never asks the server for a route.
#
# NOTE: a route added to src/AppRoutes.tsx but not to site-routes.json is not prerendered, so a
# direct visit to it would land here and 404. Add new routes to both.
/*  /404.html  404
